range throat level 0.21 0.3 the tear's voice: a drone at C2 sung like overtone (throat) singing: an arc firing at the note, each pulse a long damped sine at one harmonic
range throat formant 19 38 which harmonic it sings (3rd to 9th of C2), stepped along the overtone series by the orb's reach
range drone level 0.084 0.12 the heavy cello (C#2 tuned down to C2), level and looped: the bass, under the throat
range grind level 0 0.14 the heavy guitar, its partials pulled onto C and G, driven: grows with the machine
range breath level 0.02 0.1 the void's wind: noise through a slowly wandering bandpass, in with stir
range breath flange_pos 0.02667 0.56
range root level 0 0.09 C4: a resonator. Random impulses ring a damped sine at the note.
range root jitter 0 0.8 how the resonator is struck: at random at coherence 0 (a grainy shimmer around the note), in step at 1
range root burst 4 16 how long each strike rings, in ms: short and breathy at coherence 0, long and pure at 1: the resonance takes hold
range root ph_pos 0 1 the phaser notch, parked by the orb's curl
range third level 0 0.078 E4
range fifth level 0 0.078 G4
range seventh level 0 0.063 Bb4
range choir level 0 1 the synth vocal an octave down as six voices that roam up to 5 st off: an unearthly choir, growing with the machine
range choir gather 0.15 1 the voices converge on the chord as the ratios come in tune
range cloud level 0 0.15 a soft chord at C4, growing with the machine; spells raise it and pick the chord
range cloud voices 4 8
range cloud gather 0.5 1
bind stir throat level 0.3 0.21
bind orb.radius throat formant 19 38 scale=overtones
bind orb.accel throat flicker 0.2 0.7
bind stir breath level 0.02 0.1
bind orb.radius breath cutoff 0.4 0.7
bind tone.root root level 0 0.09
bind tone.third third level 0 0.078
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.078
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.063
bind coherence root jitter 0.8 0.12
bind coherence root burst 4 16
bind fit root flicker 0.5 0
bind orb.curl root ph_pos 0 1
bind orb.radius root cutoff 0.6 1
bind coherence third jitter 0.8 0.12
bind coherence third burst 4 16
bind fit third flicker 0.5 0
bind orb.curl third ph_pos 0 1
bind orb.radius third cutoff 0.6 1
bind coherence fifth jitter 0.8 0.12
bind coherence fifth burst 4 16
bind fit fifth flicker 0.5 0
bind orb.curl fifth ph_pos 0 1
bind orb.radius fifth cutoff 0.6 1
bind coherence seventh jitter 0.8 0.12
bind coherence seventh burst 4 16
bind fit seventh flicker 0.5 0
bind orb.curl seventh ph_pos 0 1
bind orb.radius seventh cutoff 0.6 1
bind stack choir level 0 1
bind coherence choir gather 0.15 1
bind radiance choir reverb 0.5 0.9
bind orb.speed choir speed 0.4 1
bind stack cloud level 0 0.15
bind coherence cloud gather 0.5 1
bind stack cloud voices 4 8
bind stir drone level 0.12 0.084
bind orb.radius drone cutoff 0.45 0.8
bind orb.accel drone drive 0.15 0.4
bind stack grind level 0 0.14
bind orb.radius grind cutoff 0.5 0.9
bind hand.fit grind level 0 0.1 rel
note resonant_heavy (variant, 2026-10-03): resonant with the user's distorted strings. The heavy cello is the bass under the throat (the sine sub is off), the choir is six
note cellos roaming up to 6 st off the chord until coherence gathers them, the heavy guitar is a driven wash on C and G that grows with the machine,
note and the resonators keep a quarter of their crack and are driven. The pads were made from samples/_originals by tools/padloop.py.
note resonant v1 (draft, 2026-10-03): pure anima, the family that works the Spire's machines. Raw resonance seeping in through a tear: nothing here is an element,
note so the idiom is resonance itself. Everything pitched is a resonator being struck, or a voice.
note alive = the throat: an overtone-singing drone at C2 (the orb's reach steps which harmonic it sings), a sine under it, the void's wind.
note notes = four resonators at C4 E4 G4 Bb4 (tone.*): an arc with ring 1 and formant 0 is a damped sine at the note, struck by impulses.
note in tune = the resonance takes hold: the strikes fall into step (jitter 0.8 -> 0) and ring longer (burst 5 -> 28 ms), so a grainy shimmer around the note
note becomes a pure tone (measured: 9 % of the energy within 50 cents of the note at one end, 100 % at the other, level within 5 dB). fit steadies the flicker.
note The alien part: a choir made from luminal's synth vocal an octave down, its six voices roaming up to 5 st off the chord until coherence gathers them.
note One-shots: a plucked low fifth on lock, a plucked C5 on accept (a pluck is a resonator too), a falling fifth on unlock.
note Spells are placeholders. To try next: a bowed-metal or singing-bowl recording as the choir's source instead of the vocal luminal already uses.
note Reach hint: hand.fit (the reach of the component in hand against the recipe the stations point to) adds a little to one layer when it is right, and nothing otherwise; fit steadies the voices.
note Recipes are the sigil generator's (seed 1, 2026-10-03). Spell notes that name ratios or chord tones describe the earlier, hand-made recipes.

